 "reads": [
  {
   "id": "R1",
   "text": "the anchor reproduces: on all 52 periods the funded gap is 2.87pp (IM minus ETF), against the 286.66pp r2036 published -- the cut below starts from the same number, so this face is a decomposition and not a re-derivation"
  },
  {
   "id": "R2",
   "text": "cut in half, the two halves agree: 3.04pp (first_half) and 2.69pp (second_half) on the annualised ruler, 6.85pp / 5.99pp on the cumulative one"
  },
  {
   "id": "R3",
   "text": "and the parent's own in-sample / out-of-sample split agrees with the headline: 6.08pp in sample and 6.75pp out of it (cumulative), so the flip is not an artefact of the fitted part of the window"
  },
  {
   "id": "R4",
   "text": "the 4 quarter blocks (13 periods each) run Q1 3.35pp, Q2 2.95pp, Q3 5.08pp, Q4 0.63pp -- 4 of 4 favour the futures leg; the annualised numbers on a 13-period block are noisy by construction, which is why the sign test below uses the cumulative one"
  },
  {
   "id": "R4b",
   "text": "the flip is stable in sign and shrinking in size: the last block (2025-10-16 .. 2026-11-11) pays 0.61pp against a median block of 3.05pp, and it is the only block inside the 1.0pp tie band -- a reader who trades the flip forward is trading a gap that has been narrowing for a year"
  },
  {
   "id": "R5",
   "text": "27 rolling 26-period windows (stride 1) put the futures leg in front in 27 of them (100.00%); the cumulative gap runs 3.32pp .. 11.05pp with a median of 7.02pp, so the full-window number is a middle case and not the best window"
  },
  {
   "id": "R6",
   "text": "period by period the futures leg wins 34 of 52 (65.38%) with a two-sided binomial p of 0.0365 -- a real bias, not a coin"
  },
  {
   "id": "R7",
   "text": "the drop-one jackknife moves the gap by at most 0.56pp (dropping 2025-06-18) and the gap stays positive in all of the 52 single-period removals -- the headline does not rest on a single observation"
  },
  {
   "id": "R8",
   "text": "sweeping the collateral's declared yield from 0.00% to 10.00% moves the gap from 3.24pp to 1.30pp -- the flip survives the whole range"
  },
  {
   "id": "R9",
   "text": "the frozen cash would have to earn 16.34% a year for the two carriers to tie, against a funded book return of 9.39% -- the collateral assumption r2036 could not observe cannot overturn the conclusion, because no broker pays above the book"
  }
 ],
